                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "1fb4c4a1-7518-3308-979c-2874da7e1b6b",
                        "entry_id": "97b9b986-9997-3e17-889b-7c434aa11d6d",
                        "glosses": [
                            "приписывать кому-либо или чему-либо свойства человека, наделять человеческими качествами (неодушевлённые предметы, животных и т. п.)"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "cff5794a-2e48-3ed5-b348-3edd14204190",
                        "entry_id": "97b9b986-9997-3e17-889b-7c434aa11d6d",
                        "glosses": [
                            "развивать в ком-либо человеческое начало или превращать в человека; делать более человечным, похожим на человека"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "c090cded-cf27-4a8a-8400-555e9fa0b46a",
                        "source_entry_id": "97b9b986-9997-3e17-889b-7c434aa11d6d",
                        "target_lang_word": "humanize",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "humanize",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b6e44b06-ad17-3f27-978d-e5e5ee3dce1e",
                                        "entry_id": "cd35e4f6-ccd7-36b3-b383-1c7acf119506",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To make human; to give or cause to have the fundamental properties of a human."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "990828fe-8bde-4a09-852d-3e992cc93bbc",
                                                "sense_id": "b6e44b06-ad17-3f27-978d-e5e5ee3dce1e",
                                                "text": "VVas it the buſineſs of magic to humanize our natures with compaſſion, forgiveneſs, and all the inſtances of the moſt extenſive charity?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ee4d1b91-9d6c-46f3-bc2d-a39f6f7a4386",
                                                "sense_id": "b6e44b06-ad17-3f27-978d-e5e5ee3dce1e",
                                                "text": "A waiter brought his aperitif, which was a small scotch and soda, and as he sipped it gratefully he sighed.\n ‘Civilized,’ he said to Mr. Campion. ‘Humanizing.’ […] ‘Cigars and summer days and women in big hats with swansdown face-powder, that's what it reminds me of.’"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e8c7b611-6b05-3c4a-ab5d-91dc58732871",
                                        "entry_id": "cd35e4f6-ccd7-36b3-b383-1c7acf119506",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To make sympathetic or relatable."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a8419a65-2b8a-436a-934d-1cecfcf8108a",
                                                "sense_id": "e8c7b611-6b05-3c4a-ab5d-91dc58732871",
                                                "text": "I think they would try to humanize the worst villains in history out of their fear that the audience might not like the central character."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "69de7648-079a-4a08-ae3e-86e738b3a1d8",
                                                "sense_id": "e8c7b611-6b05-3c4a-ab5d-91dc58732871",
                                                "text": "The Oscar-winning film The Iron Lady humanised Thatcher."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "51c93d22-a951-4347-9215-ab658ae58d47",
                                                "sense_id": "e8c7b611-6b05-3c4a-ab5d-91dc58732871",
                                                "text": "Like the three ceremonial functions based on the Constitutions, these informal chief of state activities emphasize the president's role as the leader of the nation, but many of them also serve to humanize the president and symbolically bridge the gap between the president and the people."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "68d0709a-0874-497b-8009-1511dae22b15",
                                                "sense_id": "e8c7b611-6b05-3c4a-ab5d-91dc58732871",
                                                "text": "We can also expect the company to continue to humanize data in creative ways like it did when it used its vast amounts of data to launch a global ad campaign that highlighted some of the more bizarre user habits of 2016."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "db83586c-1d63-37fe-a6e6-6f9fec58cbe8",
                                        "entry_id": "cd35e4f6-ccd7-36b3-b383-1c7acf119506",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To convert into something human or belonging to humans."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "05be9700-8a57-4ccc-8560-33df5bc7cf9d",
                                                "sense_id": "db83586c-1d63-37fe-a6e6-6f9fec58cbe8",
                                                "text": "to humanize vaccine lymph"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b1ac181f-1a50-4b1d-bbef-079e32a58c1b",
                                                "sense_id": "db83586c-1d63-37fe-a6e6-6f9fec58cbe8",
                                                "text": "humanized monoclonal antibodies"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "humanize",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "dd89f282-6bd7-3959-9e5a-9f99cd52e716",
                                        "entry_id": "eaa4a110-f7e2-36a3-8f05-98dfef66a5c4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To make humane."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "de7b876b-a030-4988-9e81-cdf38f7f4bdf",
                                                "sense_id": "dd89f282-6bd7-3959-9e5a-9f99cd52e716",
                                                "text": "In China, as in India, Buddhism humanized the government and the people. It was a Chinese Emperor, Ming-Ti (a.d. 58-76), converted to Buddhism that abolished the penalty of death."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "edbae566-c423-4a07-8988-cf0e6bd3a04e",
                                                "sense_id": "dd89f282-6bd7-3959-9e5a-9f99cd52e716",
                                                "text": "And consequently he humanized the company. He instituted excellent employee benefits."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5255a324-6f37-4c02-810b-c3de7790337f",
                                                "sense_id": "dd89f282-6bd7-3959-9e5a-9f99cd52e716",
                                                "text": "Some leftists believed that Cardenas humanized the government and harmonized its workings with the needs of the common people at the same time that peasant and worker activists placed demands on the political system."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f32fc375-13ca-36f6-8ce7-ee272ab9221a",
                                        "entry_id": "eaa4a110-f7e2-36a3-8f05-98dfef66a5c4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To become humane or civilized."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
